---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ToolAccessGate from "../components/ToolAccessGate.astro";
import "../styles/barcode-tools.css";
const schema = {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebApplication",name:"BarcodeNest Barcode Scanner",applicationCategory:"UtilitiesApplication",operatingSystem:"Any",url:"https://barcodenest.com/barcode-scanner/",description:"Read UPC, EAN, Code 128, QR and Data Matrix from a photo or camera capture. Account required."};
---
<BaseLayout title="Online Barcode Scanner & Image Reader | BarcodeNest" description="Scan a barcode with your phone camera or upload a PNG, JPEG or WebP. Read UPC, EAN, Code 128, QR and Data Matrix, then look up a product. Free account required." structuredData={schema} current="scanner">
  <header class="tool-hero container"><div class="eyebrow">Barcode scanner</div><h1>From a photo to a barcode number.</h1><p class="lede">Read a product barcode, inventory label or QR code. Upload an image or capture a photo, then copy the result, find product details or create a fresh barcode.</p></header>
  <ToolAccessGate />
  <div class="tool-grid container">
    <section class="tool-card">
      <h2>Scan an image</h2><p>Keep the whole barcode and its white margins in view. A sharp, well-lit image works best.</p>
      <form id="scanner-form"><fieldset data-account-tool disabled>
        <label for="scan-file">Barcode photo</label><input id="scan-file" type="file" accept="image/png,image/jpeg,image/webp" aria-describedby="scan-file-hint" />
        <p class="tool-hint" id="scan-file-hint">PNG, JPEG or WebP, up to 12 MiB. Large photos are resized before scanning.</p>
        <div class="tool-actions"><button type="submit" class="button button-signal" id="scan-upload">Read image · 1 scan</button><button type="button" class="button button-secondary" id="start-camera">Use camera</button></div>
        <div id="camera-panel" hidden><video id="scan-video" autoplay playsinline muted aria-label="Camera preview"></video><div class="tool-actions"><button type="button" class="button button-signal" id="capture-camera">Capture & read · 1 scan</button><button type="button" class="button button-secondary" id="stop-camera">Stop camera</button></div><p class="tool-hint">Only the frame you capture is sent for scanning.</p></div>
      </fieldset></form>
      <p id="scan-status" class="tool-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
      <p id="scan-balance" class="tool-hint">Sign in to see your scan allowance.</p>
      <p class="tool-hint">Each accepted image uses one scan, including images with no readable barcode. Scans have a separate allowance. Product lookups use lookup credits only when you choose to look up a result.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="tool-card" aria-labelledby="scan-result-heading"><h2 id="scan-result-heading">Decoded barcodes</h2><p id="scan-empty">Your results will appear here. QR content is shown as text so you can review it before using it.</p><div id="scan-results" aria-live="polite"></div></section>
  </div>
  <section class="tool-reference narrow"><h2>One scanner, several workflows</h2><p><a href="/blog/scan-barcode-from-image/">Read the step-by-step barcode photo scanning guide</a>.</p><p>Read EAN-13, EAN-8 and UPC-A on retail packaging, Code 128 inventory labels, and QR or Data Matrix codes. A readable barcode identifies its encoded content; product details depend on catalog coverage. This tool does not grade print quality or verify GS1 ownership.</p><h2>Separate monthly scan limits</h2><div class="comparison-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Monthly scan allowances" tabindex="0"><table class="tool-table"><thead><tr><th>Free / One-time</th><th>Creator</th><th>Starter</th><th>Growth</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>50 scans</td><td>500 scans</td><td>2,000 scans</td><td>5,000 scans</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Website and API scans share your account allowance, which resets on the first day of each month at 00:00 UTC. Creator includes scanning and creation; product lookup requires Free credits, a lookup pack, Starter or Growth.</p><h2>What happens to my photo?</h2><p>The selected image or captured frame is sent to BarcodeNest for decoding. Scanner images are processed in memory and are not saved to your account. The camera starts only when you select Use camera and stops when you close it or leave this page.</p><h2>Why was no barcode found?</h2><p>Try a closer photo with even lighting, avoid reflections, and include the full barcode. Rotate the package so the label is flat and in focus. Unsupported formats and damaged codes may not decode. You can also enter the number in the <a href="/barcode-validator/">barcode validator</a>.</p><div class="tool-links"><a href="/barcode-generator/">Create barcodes</a><a href="/barcode-labels/">Print labels</a><a href="/docs/barcode-tools/#scan-images">Image reader API</a><a href="/pricing/">Compare plans</a></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<script src="../scripts/barcode-scanner.ts"></script>
<style>
  #camera-panel{margin-top:24px}video{display:block;width:100%;max-height:360px;background:var(--ink);border-radius:6px}#scan-results :global(article){padding:20px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}#scan-results :global(pre){white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;max-height:240px;overflow:auto;padding:16px;background:var(--paper-2);font-size:16px}#scan-results :global(.scan-product){padding:12px;background:var(--paper-2);overflow-wrap:anywhere}#scan-results :global(button),#scan-results :global(a.button){min-height:44px}input[type=file]{max-width:100%}
</style>
